# Build-context hygiene.
#
# The Go stage runs `COPY . .`, so every file here would otherwise become part of
# a layer (and part of the context Docker sends to the daemon on each build).
#
# Keep: ui/ and web/ sources (the front-end stage copies them), deploy/, and the
# module's own sources.

# Version control
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules

# Documentation and CI — the image is built by Jenkins, not from the context
doc/
docs/
.github/

# Build and test output
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.html
/bin/
/out/

# Test sources: L1 runs them from the checkout, and `go build` never compiles
# them, so they do not belong in the context.
*_test.go
**/*_test.go

# Go workspace files (per-developer; would override module resolution)
go.work
go.work.sum

# Local state and secrets
.env
*.secret.json
deploy/*.local

# Editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
